[E0436] Error: `words` is used after `owned`, which it borrows, was changed
   ╭─[ err/174_adapted_views/main.wip:8:13 ]
   │
 6 │     var words = owned.split(" ").map(own (w) => w.len())
   │         ──┬──
   │           ╰──── `words` borrows `owned`
 7 │     owned.clear()
   │     ──┬──
   │       ╰──── `owned` passed as `&var` here
 8 │     val n = words.count()
   │             ──┬──
   │               ╰──── used here
   │
   │ Help: use `words` before `owned` changes, or keep a value that owns its data
   │
   │ Note: a view points into what it borrows — a `str` into bytes, a `&` into a place — so that must not change while the view is still used
